    "result_text": "Tests pass and the build is green. I agreed with all four findings and applied them:\n\n1. **Moved the derivation into `saveOwner`** \u2014 `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` are now computed inside `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`'s `if (owner.isNew())` block, right alongside `countNamesakes`, matching the established `namesakeCount` pattern. Guarded by `owner.getPossibleDuplicate() == null` so a pre-set value is respected, mirroring the `namesakeCount` guard.\n\n2. **Dropped it from the public interface** \u2014 removed `findPossibleDuplicateOf` (and its Javadoc) from `ClinicService`; it's now a private helper in `ClinicServiceImpl` next to `countNamesakes`/`countOwnersInCity`, since the controller never branches on it.\n\n3. **Unified the business rule** \u2014 the controller no longer touches these fields at all; both the id and its derived boolean (`id != null`) are now set together in the service, so \"a null id means not a possible duplicate\" lives in one place.\n\n4. **Used the imported `Objects`** \u2014 added `import java.util.Objects;` and replaced the fully-qualified `java.util.Objects.equals(...)` with `Objects.equals(...)`.\n\nThe controller's `addOwner` is back to its original shape, with all the new behaviour now encapsulated in the service layer.",
