        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe feature works at the right altitude in most respects (schema across all dialects, OpenAPI read-only fields, entity fields placed in sensible order), but the derivation logic is put in the wrong unit and is inconsistent with an established pattern already in this codebase.\n\n**1. (Main) The \"computed-once-at-creation\" derivation belongs in `saveOwner`, not the controller.**\n`possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` are the direct structural analogue of `namesakeCount`: a persisted, read-only field computed once, by comparing the not-yet-saved owner against the existing owners, at creation time. The codebase already has a home for exactly this: `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` does it under `if (owner.isNew())`, calling the private helper `countNamesakes` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:261-263`, `273-281`). The change instead scatters the equivalent work into `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:131-133`), setting two entity fields in the controller. A maintainer would expect to find this derivation sitting next to `countNamesakes` inside `saveOwner`, guarded by `owner.isNew()`, not in the controller. Move it there:\n- Add a private helper in the impl (mirroring `countNamesakes`/`countOwnersInCity`, which are private) that resolves the matching owner id.\n- Set both fields inside `saveOwner`'s `isNew()` block (e.g. `owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(id); owner.setPossibleDuplicate(id != null);`).\n\n**2. `findPossibleDuplicateOf` should not be on the public `ClinicService` interface.**\n`isIdentityKeyInUse`/`isCityAtCapacity` are public interface methods because the controller must branch on them to pick an HTTP status (CONFLICT). `findPossibleDuplicateOf` drives no such decision \u2014 the controller merely copies its result into fields that get persisted. It has no reason to be public API; like `countNamesakes` and `countOwnersInCity` it should be a private helper in `ClinicServiceImpl`. The interface + Javadoc addition in `ClinicService.java` is surface that can be dropped once the logic moves into `saveOwner`.\n\n**3. Minor: deriving the boolean in the controller splits one fact across two layers.**\n`owner.setPossibleDuplicate(possibleDuplicateOf != null)` places the \"a null id means not a possible duplicate\" business rule in the controller. Once (1) is done, both the id and its derived boolean are set together in the service, keeping the rule in one place.\n\n**4. Minor, idiomatic: use the imported `Objects`.**\n`ClinicServiceImpl.java:379` writes `java.util.Objects.equals(...)` fully qualified inline, while the file imports its other `java.util` types (`Collection`, `List`, `Map`, lines 33-36). Add `import java.util.Objects;` and call `Objects.equals(...)` to match the file's style."
